  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 13</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ se ðe utlages weorc gewyrce, wealde se cingc þæs friþes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-a">And se ðe útlages weorc gewyrce, wealde se cyningc þæs friðes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-q">Et qui opus útlagii fecerit, eius reuocatio sit in misericordia regis (pacis emendatio in solius regis consistat imperio).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="13" corresp="#wit-b">Utlaga. Se ðe útlages weorc gewyrce wealde se cyng ðæs friðes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">Outlawry. If anyone does the deed of an outlaw, the king alone shall have power to grant him security.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And if anyone commits a deed punishable by outlawry, the king [alone] is to have power to grant him peace.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Friedloser. B) Und wer Friedlosenwerk verübt: [da] verfüge der König über den Frieden [den jener sich wiederkaufe].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Outlaw. B) And whoever commits a deed that incurs outlawry: let the king decide on his [being restored to the] peace.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">B's heading ‘Utlaga’ is red.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
